Game reference data in packages/engine/src/game/genshin/data.generated.json is derived from the
genshin-db project (https://github.com/theBowja/genshin-db) at build time.
Genshin Impact and all related data are property of HoYoverse. This project bundles
only numeric stat/reference data for interoperability; no game assets are included.
Data snapshot: see the "genshinDbVersion", "gameVersion" and "generatedAt" fields in
data.generated.json.

## Meta build recipes

The "meta build" recipes in `packages/engine/src/meta/metaTargets.ts` (recommended set, main stats,
and stat targets per character) are hand-adapted from the community guides at
KQM (KeqingMains, https://keqingmains.com). They are summaries of public guidance,
not copied text, and are used as an optional, overridable comparison target. Genshin
Impact and all related data are property of HoYoverse.

## Combat rotations

The rotations in `rotations/` and the gcsim configs they produce use community simulation
configs from the KQM Sim Database (KeqingMains, https://db.kqm.gg; formerly gcsim's own
database). Credit goes to KQM and the configs' submitters. Each rotation names its entry
(`source.url` in its `meta.json`, and the header of its `reference.gcsl`), and the
published assumptions are kept as they are: the action list, the reference builds, the
target and the energy drops. Only character names are turned into placeholders; a
rotation adapted for another team is marked `draft` and says what was changed. The
curated "Mualani Burn-Vape" comp archetype also comes from a KQM Sim Database entry.

Simulations run on gcsim (https://github.com/genshinsim/gcsim, AGPL-3.0 since v2.48) as
an unmodified external program downloaded at a pinned version; no gcsim source is
included in this repository.
